From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:40:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Transfer worker attachment bytes through verified
 Board storage

Why: row sync dropped machine-local stored_path while no blob transfer consumed the metadata, stranding completion artifacts on workers.

How: bounded authenticated binary transfers, durable cursor-independent retries, atomic verified hydration of live and replica stores, and eviction custody until storage acknowledgment.

Proof: original transport/offline archive regressions fail before the fix; focused sync/worker consumers pass; 19 byte-custody and HTTP tests pass and all eight targeted mutants are killed. Actual worker completion deletes scratch while home reads artifact bytes. Partial chunked HTTP and populated-path corruption findings are red/green covered. Service API deployment is separately owned by t_01a1cca4c35fbeeb.
